course: dictionary
lesson: 3134
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the clues around them to choose the right one. «The elves in the story helped the shoemaker finish his shoes at night.» The words story and helped show that elves here are magical creatures from a folk tale.
explain: «Santa's elves work hard all year to make toys at the North Pole.» Now the clues are Santa, toys and the North Pole, so elves are helpers at Christmas. The same word, two different meanings. Always ask: what does the sentence tell me about this word?
explain: The word elf is for a made-up creature, not a real one. But it can also be part of the name of a real bird. «The elf owl of the deserts of the USA and Mexico weighs about 40 grams, about as much as a sparrow.» Here the clues say the bird is real, so elf is a name, not magic.
fact: An elf is a small magical creature in stories and folk tales, often with pointed ears.
fact: In Christmas stories, elves are Santa's helpers who make toys at the North Pole.
fact: In fantasy books and games, elves are tall, wise and live very long.
fact: Elves are made up, so they are not real, but some real animals have elf in their name, such as the elf owl.
fact: «Elf ears» and «elf on the shelf» are phrases you may hear at Christmas.
exercise: In «The elves helped the shoemaker finish his shoes», what are the elves? | Sheep farmers | Tall dark trees | Real people who wear shoes | *Small magical creatures in stories
exercise: In «Santa's elves make toys at the North Pole», where do the elves work? | *At the North Pole | Under the sea | In a school | In a shop in town
exercise: The elf owl «weighs about 40 grams, about as much as a sparrow». Is the elf owl a real bird or a made-up creature? | *A real bird | A Christmas toy | A tall, wise person | A made-up creature in a story
test: In fantasy books, elves are described as tall and very wise. What kind of elves are these? | Tricky creatures with pointed ears | *Tall, wise people who live very long | Real owls | Christmas helpers who make toys
test: The name elf is used for a real bird in «the elf owl». What does the sentence tell you about this use of the word? | It is a Christmas story | *The bird is real, so elf is part of its name | It is about magic | It is a made-up creature
exam: Which meaning of elf is used in «Santa's elves make toys at the North Pole»? | A tall, wise person who lives very long | A real owl | *Santa's helper who makes toys | A magic creature in a fantasy game
